WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.050
In October 2022, prices
in the UK were rising

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.860
at 11.1 per cent a year.

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.220
By May 2024, that rate
was down to 2 per cent.

4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.280
Yet prices had not fallen.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.080
They kept rising, just more slowly.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.290
Each month, that single rate
sums up about 180,000 prices,

7
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.340
collected all over the country.

8
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.580
So how can one number tell you how much

9
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.870
prices have risen for a
whole country of shoppers?

10
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.610
In this mission, you'll build
a price index step by step,

11
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.340
and calculate an inflation rate yourself.

12
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.240
Then you'll turn money
values into real ones,

13
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.140
and see where the official
measure can mislead.

14
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.350
Your mission: find out
how inflation is measured,

15
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.370
and how far to trust the number.
